  "location": "CRE52.50",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: CRE52.50",
      "summary": "CRE52.50 defines the margin period of risk by reference to CRE50.18, which defines the margin threshold; the MPOR definition is CRE50.19.",
      "impact": "Position: Margined netting set, daily VM, bank estimates MPOR 15 business days; trade effective notional d*delta = 1000. Reading a: Following the intended CRE50.19 definition: MPOR 15 days, higher than floor 10, MF = 1.5*sqrt(15/250) = 0.367, D = 367 Reading b: Following CRE50.18 literally: no MPOR definition applies to estimate, bank uses only the floor of 10 days, MF = 0.300, D = 300 Difference: effective notional 67 (about 22%)",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
